-- re-embed marker: 2026-06-01u — v0.15.55 Cycle 7 F1: cross-axis HEIGHT fill in row parents (`heightFillFor AsRow`) strips the `height: 100%` emission, keeping only `align-self: stretch;`. Per CSS Flexbox §9.8 the `100%` was redundant when the row's cross-axis (height) was definite AND ACTIVELY HARMFUL when it was flex-grow-derived (indefinite) — the `100%` collapses to auto/content, defeating the stretch and producing the user-reported 22 px / 51 px collapses in #63 (three-pane app shell + Input.multiline). Asymmetric scope: cross-axis WIDTH fill in column / el / textColumn parents KEEPS the `width: 100%` because column-parent widths are typically definite (block inheritance from <body>) AND the explicit `width: 100%` protects against the F4 interaction (`[Ui.width fill, Ui.centerX]` where `align-self: center` cascades over the stretch, leaving width to fall back to content). Width-fill in row parents (main axis) is unchanged: `flex-grow + min-width: 0`. Touches `heightFillFor` in `sky-stdlib/Std/Ui.sky` only. Regression: scripts/verify-stdui-matrix.mjs (Z2 textarea ≥ 760 px tall, Z3 sidebar/main/content ≥ 700 px) + UiFillCssSpec.hs.
